South Korean Experts Blame North Korea for Aggression, Not Aggression Tact: Was the Korean War Inevitable?

According to a report in The Diplomat, a leading South Korean think tank, Professor Emeritus Kim, Director of the Institute for Peace and Unification Studies at Seoul  Korea University, blamed North Korea for the outbreak of the Korean War. He was quoted as saying, "The Korean War was not an unjust war of aggression by the South but a just war of self-defense by the North."

Another South Korean experts also pointed out that the North had violatedInninguished a ceasefire agreement and launched a surprise attack on the South in 1950.

